Qualcomm's Vulkan driver before 512.616 (the Beam Pro's Adreno 710 has 512.615) draws a render pass
of several draws wrongly when its first draw does not reach every one of the columns the driver
splits the pass into: later draws in such a column land at the first column's place, or over what
the memory held. Pages showed other tiles' content in the row under their header (2026-11-14, on
Chromium 153 and 157 alike). ANGLE draws over the whole render area before a pass's second draw,
blended so as to change nothing, for that driver alone (drawWholeRenderAreaBeforeSecondDraw).
Measured headless: pages equal to software raster's; 5 to 9 per cent of the frame rate.

